Back to You
===========

This repository is covered by TWO licenses. Read this before assuming MIT
applies to everything in it.

  Code, scripts, documentation, and artwork        MIT License (below)
      install.bat, install.sh, install.command, hooks/, tools/, tests/,
      assets/, and every .md file including ELEVENLABS-VOICE-PROMPT.md

  Audio files under sounds/                        NOT open source
      See LICENSE-AUDIO. Redistribution and modification are permitted,
      for NON-COMMERCIAL use only.

Third-party material used under its own terms is listed in NOTICE. That is
currently one item: the banner wordmark is drawn as outlines derived from
Roboto Medium, which is Apache-2.0.

Why the split: the shipped voice clips were generated with ElevenLabs,
whose Prohibited Use Policy forbids offering their output under terms more
permissive than ElevenLabs' own. MIT is more permissive, so it cannot apply
to the audio. The code carries no such restriction and is MIT with no
asterisks.

Note that ELEVENLABS-VOICE-PROMPT.md is MIT, deliberately. It is a complete
recipe for regenerating the pack. Anyone who wants this audio without the
restrictions in LICENSE-AUDIO can generate their own under their own
ElevenLabs account and own the result outright.

